   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the banking law, in relation to notice of the posting of the\nwhat mortgage applicants need to know pamphlet on residential mortgages and\nmodification of such pamphlet",
    "basePrintNo": "S767",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S767-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §35, Bank L (as proposed in S.5597-B & A.9686)",
    "lawSection": "Banking Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S767\n\nSPONSOR: COMRIE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the banking law, in relation to notice of the posting of\nthe what mortgage applicants need to know pamphlet on residential mort-\ngages and modification of such pamphlet\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis chapter amendment makes changes to the provisions L.2024 c.566,\nrequiring the Department of Financial Services to develop and distribute\na \"what mortgage applicants need to know\" pamphlet.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one amends the underlying chapter in the banking law requiring\nthe Department of Financial Services (DFS) to develop a pamphlet for\nprospective mortgage holders to require that DFS notify licensed mort-\ngage bankers when such pamphlet is available and to allow DFS to make\nchanges to the pamphlet at as needed to conform with applicable federal\nand state law.\n\nSection two includes the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation ensures the public's awareness of the \"what mortgage\napplicants need to know.\" This legislation will serve as another tool to\nassist New Yorkers with homebuying, which can be confusing on the first\ntime or for those planning to buy and have not done so in a long time.\nRegardless, having access to this information will inevitably assist\nanyone looking to buy a home. This bill requires the mortgage pamphlet\nbe translated in the state's most spoken languages to ensure consumer\nunderstanding among those with limited English proficiency.\n\nIt is important to have access to this information before closing, as\ninterest rates and market comparisons may help influence the agreed.\nupon cost and save New Yorkers money over the long run. In addition,\nlenders may not be as forthcoming as consumers may believe in the inter-\nest of writing mortgages, even when rates are less than ideal.\n\nThis bill amends L.2024 c.566 creating a \"what mortgage applicants need\nto know\" pamphlet. This bill is a negotiated change to the underlying\nchapter.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis bill amends Chapter 566 of the Laws of 2024. S.5597-B and A.9686\npassed the Senate and Assembly in May 2024.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the same date and in the same manner as\nchapter 566 of the laws of 2024 amending the banking law relating to\nwhat mortgage applicants need to know pamphlet on residential mortgages,\nas proposed in legislative bills numbers S.5597-B and A.9686, takes\neffect.\n",
